== Trivia ==
*Mithril is a fictional material originating from J.R.R Tolkien's Middle Earth universe. Dwarves forged it into armor that cannot be pierced by even the strongest blades. This is referenced not only shown by the name of the Dwarven Metal but also by the {{Item|Mithril Coat}}, a direct reference to Tolkien's Middle-earth Mithril.
**This material also appears in Terraria, albeit spelled ''Mythril''<ref>[[terraria:Mythril_Ore]]</ref>, rather than Mithril.
*Inside the {{Zone|Dwarven Mines}} and {{zone|Glacite Tunnels}}, only the Mithril in the texture of {{Item|Gray Wool|link=}} and {{Item|Cyan Hardened Clay|link=}} can be insta-mined. {{Item|Light Blue Wool|link=}} Mithril cannot be insta-mined, even inside the {{Zone|Crystal Hollows}}.

